  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h4 id="thag1.118" class="h1">Thag 1:118  Kimbila</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>As if sent by a curse,<span class="fn"><a href="#thag1.118note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
              <p>it drops on us—</p>
              <p class="v4">aging.</p>
              <p>The body seems     other,</p>
              <p>though it’s still the same one.</p>
              <p>I’m still here</p>
              <p>&amp; have never been absent from it,</p>
              <p>but I remember myself</p>
              <p>as if somebody else’s.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="thag1.118note01">1. Reading <em>abhisatto</em> with the Sinhalese and Burmese editions. The Thai and PTS have <em>abhisattho,</em> “ordered.”</p>
            </div><!--end notes-->
            <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../Thig/thig13_1.html">Thig 13:1</a></p><!--end seealso-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
